From 6f5bf2d85864a09713c1044cf5d41de09ad8d10a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:59:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 233/233] hir_expand: lifetime inference pass limit scales with
 the ivar count

The lifetime ivar solver gave up after 1000 passes ("Lifetime inferrence
stalled"). A `&mut` method chain takes about two passes per call, so ~450
calls (`b.field(..).field(..)...`, the derive(Debug) shape) hit the cap
with work still progressing.

A pass that doesn't bail sets at least one ivar (`change` is only set in
`set()`, which asserts the ivar was unknown) and the loop allocates no new
ivars, so it ends within `ivars + 1` passes anyway; the cap is now the
larger of 1000 and that. Nothing changes for bodies that finished before.

Found with the 0232 kit (method-chain-depth-test, 500 call case); no known
crate hits it yet (skim's chain is ~150 calls).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hir_expand/lifetime_infer.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/hir_expand/lifetime_infer.cpp b/src/hir_expand/lifetime_infer.cpp
index 9b5ab49e..cb7db94e 100644
--- a/src/hir_expand/lifetime_infer.cpp
+++ b/src/hir_expand/lifetime_infer.cpp
@@ -2279,7 +2279,9 @@ namespace {
 
         // If there were inferred liftimes present
 
-        for(size_t cur_iter = 0, remaining_iters = 1000; remaining_iters--; cur_iter ++ )
+        // Each pass that doesn't bail sets at least one ivar (and none are added), so this is only a backstop. A long method
+        // chain (`b.field(..).field(..)` x 500) takes about two passes per call, scale with the ivar count.
+        for(size_t cur_iter = 0, remaining_iters = std::max<size_t>(1000, state.m_ivars.size() + 1); remaining_iters--; cur_iter ++ )
         {
             TRACE_FUNCTION_FR("=== Iter " << cur_iter << " ===", "=== Iter " << cur_iter << " ===");
             state.dump();
